recommended configuration: A3, prefix sort without compaction.
  Most tokens arrive in batches inside the single-pass window, where
  ordering repays itself with no reuse and no extra device memory.

mean stage split, ms per call
  split                       6.442
  explode                     2.675
  lookup                      4.709
  groupby                     5.935
  join                        2.127
  total                      21.889

lookup is 21.5 % of pipeline time, so the end-to-end gain
from a faster traversal is bounded by Amdahl's law:
  traversal 1.25x           1.04x end to end
  traversal 1.94x           1.12x end to end
  traversal 3.33x           1.18x end to end
  traversal made free       1.27x end to end
The 1.25x and 3.33x rows are A3 and A6 of Table 4.1; the last is
the ceiling on any possible improvement to the traversal kernel.

Stage timings are taken with the pipeline synchronized between
stages and are therefore pessimistic in total; batch sizes are not
affected. The lookup row is the kernel this study optimizes; the
others bound how much end-to-end gain any ordering can deliver.
